The Go rendering: a command that reads the fields of three configurations by
reflection through method values of Interface, Field and Elem, and asserts each
field's value to an interface it calls. A second file walks one value per shape:
direct calls, a method expression, a local that holds one of two structs, a
method value of Interface on one of two fields, a parameter of a function called
by name, a slice field walked by index, a pointer field, constant and variable
indexes, a loop over every field, an interface field, a constant field beside a
sibling the walk never reaches, and a value Interface returns that fmt prints.

